      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The vital problem with URP is that it's hard to patch on runtime, and that's how 99% of the avatars are loaded on the client and worlds as well. So VRChat would need to figure out a way to patch BiRP shaders into URP compatible, seems that URP is going to be the consolidated base that Unity will use in the future.\n\nI feel that a move to URP as soon as possible will cause less pain in the future, because currently all content in VRChat is incompatible and any new content will too be incompatible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-31T22:14:24.635Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With BiRP being deprecated in the future, is there any chance that VRChat will migrate to use URP in the future? Yes, I understand this will cause issues with existing content, so the idea I have is that there should be an open alpha branch to give creators vital time to migrate existing content to support URP.\n\nIf Beat Saber can provide a URP beta branch, why not VRChat too?",
